    "body": "Not sure if this is the same bug, or distinct.\r\nUsing ZSH, whenever I hit ctrl-R to history search, the cursor is two characters to the right of where it should be.  This persists through editing the history, and sometimes causes me to delete the wrong character in editing previous commands.  This seems to happen more frequently on multi-line commands in history, but I haven't nailed down the particulars.",
