    "updated_at": "2021-02-13T18:26:34Z",
    "body": "Same behaviour seen under certain circumstances on Linux using Bash, with GNOME Terminal and Tilix.\r\n\r\nIn my case, it turns out to be related to having emoji in the prompt - one character gets eaten for every emoji in the prompt, after arrowing up to a long history line.\r\n\r\nDisabling Starship and just setting e.g. `PS1=📦`, and then hitting the up arrow is enough to trigger the bug, regardless of the history line length. Conversely, changing to a non-emoji symbol for various modules that use emoji by default fixes it.\r\n\r\nEdit: this is with the line_break module disabled, so prompt components and hence emoji appear inline with the cursor, current history item etc. The issue doesn't occur with the line_break module enabled.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/starship/starship/issues/comments/778657498/reactions",
